        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Cast iron does not just work on induction, it is one of the best things you can put on it: strongly magnetic, efficient, and heavy enough to iron out the way induction heats in a ring. A basic Lodge skillet and an enameled Dutch oven will outperform cookware costing many times more on the jobs they are good at.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Everything that goes wrong comes down to four habits. Lift instead of sliding, keep the glass and the pan base clean, preheat gradually instead of on boost, and match the pan to the zone. Do those and the glass stays clear, the pan stays flat, and the food cooks evenly to the edge. For the full set of pieces worth owning, see our <a href="/best-induction-cookware/">best induction cookware</a> picks.
          </p>
